`canonical_form()` calls `decompose()`, and `decompose()` calls `communication_classes()`, so the suite reaches the target line through that path. In `communication_classes()`, `current_level` is incremented at the start of each `while` iteration, while `level[j]` is assigned only when `j` is first discovered as a tree edge. Thus the relation `current_level == level[i] + 1` holds for nodes being processed one BFS layer after they were assigned. But the loop reuses and rebinds `newly_visited` inside `for i in newly_visited`, so the target line can also be evaluated for states where `i` is not exactly one level behind the current counter. Therefore that equality is not guaranteed on every evaluation.

